@page "/"

<PageTitle> Snake </PageTitle>

<h1>Welcome to Mason and Sinahi's Snake Game</h1>

<p>
    This is a multiplayer online game built using Blazor and a custom network controller. It communicates with a game server to receive and display the state of the game world, including all snakes, walls, and powerups.
</p>

<h2>Design Decisions</h2>
<p>While building the Snake Game, we made several key design decisions to improve user experience and maintainability:</p>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Color Coding:</strong> Each snake is assigned a base color and an outline color based on their PlayerID to help distinguish players visually.</li>
    <li><strong>Mouse Powerup:</strong> A custom powerup mechanic where collecting desert mice causes your snake to grow in size—designed to add fun and challenge to the gameplay.</li>
    <li><strong>Player Name Truncation:</strong> Player names are limited to 16 characters. If a name is longer, it is automatically shortened to the first 13 characters followed by "...". </li>
</ul>


<h2>Features Implemented</h2>
<ul>
    <li>Opening page that indicates if it is ready to connect to the server.</li>
    <li>If there are issues connecting, a message is displayed on the canvas.</li>
    <li>Connect to a server by entering name, address, and port.</li>
    <li>Responsive to keyboard input (WASD only) to control snake direction.</li>
    <li>Disconnect button to manually exit the game server.</li>
    <li>World is not drawn if the player is not connected to avoid unnecessary rendering.</li>
</ul>

<p><em>Thanks for playing!</em></p>
